hey are not taiwan  and they are not part of taiwan  um  they are migrants so they really depend  on the support or protection given by  their home countries either from  indonesia  philippines  thailand or  vietnam  so when it comes into in a future  conflict in the taiwan strait when it  comes into evacuation plan they will  really depend on their government in  their home countries  how then the governments in jakarta for  example or in manila  protect them  evacuate them from the crisis or from  the potential conflict there's uh so far  of course when it comes to uh evacuation  plan a country will prioritize its  citizen and these workers are not  citizens in taiwan not citizens of  taiwan so they really depend on the  protection  from their own government and their  their government do not have a  diplomatic relations with taiwan when  they don't have diplomatic relations  it will cause a limited engagement it  will cause a limited direct  communication between governments and  when it comes into evacuation plan then  you need a very clear plan on how  very clear plan and communication on how  to evacuate them in which point that  they should go from their place in order  to find a safe place for them  to stay for a while while waiting for  the  uh for the flights for example to come  to save them we'll have to leave it  there for the time being thank you so  much for joining us today rati cavinava  from the university of western australia  thank you so much  you
 

